.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-AGGREGATE 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-aggregate \- prepare an experimental base/EXP ALSA configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-aggregate \-\-base\fR ID \fB\-\-expansion\fR ID [\fB\-\-write-config\fR FILE]
               [\fB\-\-bin-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect one base device (0582:0120) and one EXP device (0582:0121) by discovered identity,
for example serial:SERIAL. Emit a JSON plan after two matching clock snapshots
and repeated identity checks. Run as the regular user.
.PP
Both devices must already use the same 44100, 48000 or 96000 Hz rate.
Connect EXP COAXIAL OUT to base COAXIAL IN and enable DIGITAL AUTO on the base.
The base must report an active external-clock display. These flags do not prove clock quality.
.PP
With \fB\-\-write-config\fR, create a new mode-0600 ALSA configuration file.
Existing files and symlinks are refused. The PCM name is octa_expand:
24 capture channels, 20 playback channels, base channels first, EXP poll master,
S24_3LE with no resampling. Set ALSA_CONFIG_PATH to this file when opening the PCM.
.PP
This command does not change hardware rate, pause an audio server, install a desktop
profile or modify ~/.asoundrc automatically. Other clients must release both devices.
Regenerate after clock changes, unplug or card renumbering.
Coupled rate changes and physical pair synchronization, streaming and recovery remain unverified/incomplete.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
